    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d235">

                <pb facs="0581" n="485" xml:id="pg485"/>

                <head>No. 214.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Sir Edward Thornton to Mr.
                    Evarts</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1879-01-23"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 23, 1879</date>.
                        (Received January 24.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your note of the 20th of
                    November last, I have the honor to transmit herewith copy of a dispatch, and of
                    its inclosures, which I have received from the governor-general of Canada
                    relative to the forcible removal of the American steamtug Crusader from
                    Fairport, Dhio, to Sarnia, in Canada.</p>
                <p>I have the honor, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>EDWD. THORNTON.</signed></closer>




